{"name":"Toque White","hex":"#e7e2da","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"toque","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of hat with no brim.","A tall white hat with no brim of the sort worn by chefs."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A knitted hat, usually conical but of varying shape, often woollen, and sometimes topped by a pom-pom or tassel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toque"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Toque","blocks":[{"text":"A toque is a type of hat with a narrow brim or no brim at all."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Portrait_of_Philip_II_of_Spain_by_Sofonisba_Anguissola_-_002b.jpg/330px-Portrait_of_Philip_II_of_Spain_by_Sofonisba_Anguissola_-_002b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toque"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_conten